aystyle {\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}a{r}^{n},\n$$ it is a geometric series. \n\nTo determine the sum, we use the formula for the sum ${S}_{N}$ of a geometric series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{1}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $r=4$ and $N=5.$ We need to figure out the value of ${a}_{1}.$\n\nThe formula for the $n$th term of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{3}{2}(4)^{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore, we can calculate the first term ${a}_{1}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{3}{2}(4)^{1} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we substitute ${a}_{1}=6,r=4$ and $N=5$ into the formula for ${S}_{N}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}\\frac{3}{2}(4)^{n} & =6\\cdot \\frac{(1-{4}^{5})}{1-4} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{(-1023)}{(-3)} \\\\  & =6(341) \\\\  & =2046\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186233732 1074 "Since the given series is in the form ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}a{r}^{n},$ it is a geometric series. \n\nTo determine the sum, we use the formula for the sum ${S}_{N}$ of a geometric series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{1}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $r=4$ and $N=5.$ We need to figure out the value of ${a}_{1}.$\n\nThe formula for the $n$th term of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{3}{2}(4)^{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore, we can calculate the first term ${a}_{1}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{3}{2}(4)^{1} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we substitute ${a}_{1}=6,r=4$ and $N=5$ into the formula for ${S}_{N}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}\\frac{3}{2}(4)^{n} & =6\\cdot \\frac{(1-{4}^{5})}{1-4} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{(-1023)}{(-3)} \\\\  & =6(341) \\\\  & =2046\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186233733 1071 "Evaluate the **exact value** of the following geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\sum }_{n=1}^{4}\\frac{21}{{7}^{n}}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186233733 1071 "Evaluate the